1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,435
Iceland had no mosquitoes.

2
00:00:02,435 --> 00:00:03,584
None. Not one,

3
00:00:03,584 --> 00:00:05,390
as far as anyone knew.

4
00:00:05,885 --> 00:00:08,639
Then, in
October twenty twenty-five,

5
00:00:08,639 --> 00:00:11,471
a man in a
quiet farming area spotted

6
00:00:11,471 --> 00:00:14,225
a strange fly
on a wine-soaked rope.

7
00:00:14,727 --> 00:00:17,321
Here is how an
island of fire and ice

8
00:00:17,321 --> 00:00:19,003
lost its proudest boast,

9
00:00:19,003 --> 00:00:21,387
and what else
makes it so strange.

10
00:00:21,889 --> 00:00:22,907
Stay for the pools.

11
00:00:22,907 --> 00:00:24,889
That is where
Icelanders really live.

12
00:00:25,789 --> 00:00:27,692
Iceland sits in
the North Atlantic.

13
00:00:27,692 --> 00:00:29,868
About three
hundred ninety-four thousand

14
00:00:29,868 --> 00:00:30,792
people live here,

15
00:00:30,792 --> 00:00:32,369
and the capital is Reykjavik.

16
00:00:32,870 --> 00:00:34,818
The island covers
about one hundred

17
00:00:34,818 --> 00:00:36,654
three thousand
square kilometers,

18
00:00:36,654 --> 00:00:37,990
and much of it is empty.

19
00:00:38,688 --> 00:00:39,997
Now, the mosquitoes.

20
00:00:39,997 --> 00:00:41,634
The place is called Kjós.

21
00:00:41,634 --> 00:00:44,449
A citizen scientist
was hanging wine-soaked

22
00:00:44,449 --> 00:00:46,871
ropes to attract
moths when he caught

23
00:00:46,871 --> 00:00:47,788
a strange fly.

24
00:00:48,284 --> 00:00:49,309
Over three days,

25
00:00:49,309 --> 00:00:50,333
he caught three.

26
00:00:50,333 --> 00:00:51,934
Two females and one male.

27
00:00:52,434 --> 00:00:54,226
They probably
arrived on freight,

28
00:00:54,226 --> 00:00:56,127
and this species
can survive winter

29
00:00:56,127 --> 00:00:57,594
inside barns and basements.

30
00:00:58,089 --> 00:00:59,916
Iceland is warming
about four times

31
00:00:59,916 --> 00:01:01,794
faster than the
rest of the northern

32
00:01:01,794 --> 00:01:03,778
hemisphere. Antarctica is
now the only

33
00:01:03,778 --> 00:01:05,239
place believed to have none.

34
00:01:06,135 --> 00:01:07,073
Now, the places.

35
00:01:07,073 --> 00:01:09,417
Þingvellir is
where Iceland's parliament

36
00:01:09,417 --> 00:01:11,468
first met, in
the year nine thirty.

37
00:01:11,468 --> 00:01:13,636
It kept meeting
there until seventeen

38
00:01:13,636 --> 00:01:15,805
ninety-eight, and the
park is a World

39
00:01:15,805 --> 00:01:16,625
Heritage site.

40
00:01:17,125 --> 00:01:19,433
Not far away,
the geyser Strokkur erupts

41
00:01:19,433 --> 00:01:20,934
every five to ten minutes,

42
00:01:20,934 --> 00:01:23,242
throwing boiling water
fifteen to twenty

43
00:01:23,242 --> 00:01:23,935
meters high.

44
00:01:24,433 --> 00:01:25,518
In the southeast,

45
00:01:25,518 --> 00:01:28,134
Jökulsárlón is a
lagoon full of icebergs.

46
00:01:28,134 --> 00:01:30,559
Pieces of them wash
up on a black sand

47
00:01:30,559 --> 00:01:32,793
beach nearby,
called Diamond Beach.

48
00:01:33,691 --> 00:01:36,649
Now, culture. Icelandic
life runs on

49
00:01:36,649 --> 00:01:37,471
hot water.

50
00:01:37,973 --> 00:01:40,142
About ninety percent
of homes are heated

51
00:01:40,142 --> 00:01:41,389
with geothermal energy.

52
00:01:41,389 --> 00:01:43,503
And the same hot
water fills the pools.

53
00:01:44,006 --> 00:01:45,272
In twenty twenty-five,

54
00:01:45,272 --> 00:01:47,344
UNESCO added
Iceland's swimming pool

55
00:01:47,344 --> 00:01:50,336
culture to its list
of intangible cultural heritage.

56
00:01:50,841 --> 00:01:52,974
People of every age
sit in the hot

57
00:01:52,974 --> 00:01:54,167
tubs, in swimsuits,

58
00:01:54,167 --> 00:01:55,861
on equal footing, and talk.

59
00:01:56,360 --> 00:01:57,835
But first, the rule.

60
00:01:57,835 --> 00:01:59,458
You must shower naked,

61
00:01:59,458 --> 00:02:01,523
with soap, before you enter.

62
00:02:01,523 --> 00:02:03,810
Swimsuits only
go on afterward.

63
00:02:04,308 --> 00:02:06,275
Christmas is even stranger.

64
00:02:06,275 --> 00:02:08,970
Thirteen Yule Lads
come down from the

65
00:02:08,970 --> 00:02:10,864
mountains, one each night,

66
00:02:10,864 --> 00:02:12,758
starting December twelfth.

67
00:02:13,263 --> 00:02:15,880
Children leave a
shoe on the windowsill.

68
00:02:15,880 --> 00:02:17,646
Good kids get a small gift.

69
00:02:17,646 --> 00:02:19,543
Bad kids get a rotten potato.

70
00:02:20,041 --> 00:02:22,961
And a giant Yule
Cat eats anyone who

71
00:02:22,961 --> 00:02:25,881
has no new
clothes by Christmas Eve.

72
00:02:26,377 --> 00:02:29,259
Many Icelanders will
not rule out elves.

73
00:02:29,259 --> 00:02:31,780
The road agency
even has a standard

74
00:02:31,780 --> 00:02:33,797
reply for reporters who ask.

75
00:02:34,296 --> 00:02:35,936
Then there is hákarl.

76
00:02:35,936 --> 00:02:37,186
Greenland shark,

77
00:02:37,186 --> 00:02:40,232
fermented, then hung
to dry for months.

78
00:02:40,232 --> 00:02:41,951
It is a national dish,

79
00:02:41,951 --> 00:02:44,216
though not everyone loves it.

80
00:02:45,115 --> 00:02:47,398
Now, what does
ten dollars get you?

81
00:02:47,398 --> 00:02:50,202
The króna is
about one hundred twenty-three

82
00:02:50,202 --> 00:02:51,115
to the dollar,

83
00:02:51,115 --> 00:02:54,115
so ten dollars is
about twelve hundred krónur.

84
00:02:54,612 --> 00:02:57,098
That buys a
famous Reykjavik hot dog,

85
00:02:57,098 --> 00:02:58,441
about seven dollars,

86
00:02:58,441 --> 00:02:59,852
with a little change.

87
00:03:00,350 --> 00:03:02,445
A coffee is
about five dollars.

88
00:03:02,445 --> 00:03:05,080
A beer at a bar
is ten dollars or more.

89
00:03:05,585 --> 00:03:08,726
Sources vary, so
treat these as estimates.

90
00:03:08,726 --> 00:03:10,595
Alcohol is heavily taxed.

91
00:03:11,497 --> 00:03:13,943
One more thing
before you pack.

92
00:03:13,943 --> 00:03:15,127
The don't list.

93
00:03:15,828 --> 00:03:17,580
Don't skip the naked shower.

94
00:03:17,580 --> 00:03:19,394
Pool staff take it seriously,

95
00:03:19,394 --> 00:03:21,208
and it keeps the water clean.

96
00:03:21,704 --> 00:03:24,026
Don't turn your back
on the ocean at

97
00:03:24,026 --> 00:03:26,477
Reynisfjara. Sneaker
waves have killed

98
00:03:26,477 --> 00:03:28,864
visitors, so obey
the warning lights.

99
00:03:29,365 --> 00:03:30,833
Don't drive off-road.

100
00:03:30,833 --> 00:03:32,300
All of it is illegal,

101
00:03:32,300 --> 00:03:35,166
and fines can
reach hundreds of thousands

102
00:03:35,166 --> 00:03:35,865
of krónur.

103
00:03:36,369 --> 00:03:38,607
Don't ignore weather
and road alerts.

104
00:03:38,607 --> 00:03:40,663
A stuck vehicle
is the most common

105
00:03:40,663 --> 00:03:41,389
rescue call.

106
00:03:41,886 --> 00:03:43,883
And don't worry about tipping.

107
00:03:43,883 --> 00:03:45,215
Service is included,

108
00:03:45,215 --> 00:03:46,746
and it is not expected.

109
00:03:47,248 --> 00:03:48,250
That was Iceland.

110
00:03:48,250 --> 00:03:50,313
Which country should
we visit next?

111
00:03:50,313 --> 00:03:51,728
Tell me in the comments.
